Error [E1101]: `two` and `one` can reach the same place at the same time
  --> tests/ui/taskgroup_overlapping_write_borrows.jet:18:21
    |
 18 |         b :: g.task => {
    |                     ^^^^
 Why: a taskgroup runs its children at the same time, so two children may borrow one place only when the compiler can prove the places never overlap
 Fix: borrow separate fields or constant indexes, give each task its own owned copy, or send results back through a channel
